          %p
          #CellStructureCompatibleUnderPassingFromCToH.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Under a decomposition
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℍ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{H} \,\simeq\, \mathbb{C} \oplus \mathbb{C}^\ast
              as above, the cell structures on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+projective+spaces"} complex projective spaces
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+projective+spaces"} quaternionic projective spaces
              from Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CellStructureOfKProjectiveSpace"}
              are compatible, in that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
              we have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+diagram"} pasting diagram
              of the form
            %svg{:height => "98.86", :viewbox => "0 0 112.835 98.86", :width => "112.835", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "xmlns:xlink" => "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"}
              %defs
                %g
