            %p
              where the top square and the total rectangle are the
              = succeed "-squares" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CellStructureOfKProjectiveSpace"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the bottom left vertical morphism is the canonical projection (the “
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twistor+fibration"}> twistor fibration
                  ” for
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 1
              %li
                %p
                  the bottom right vertical morphism is the canonical inclusion
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℂ
                        %msup
                          %mi P
                          %mrow
                            %mn 2
                            %mi k
                            %mo +
                            %mn 2
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi ℂ
                        %msup
                          %mi P
                          %mrow
                            %mn 2
                            %mi k
                            %mo +
                            %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^{2k + 2} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{C}P^{2k+3}
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CanonicalInclusionsOfProjectiveSpacesByInsertingZeroOnTheRight"} (1)
                  followed by that canonical projection.
            %p
              In particular, it follows by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
              that this bottom square is also a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
            %p
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p First, the bottom left morphism clearly has to be the claimed projection for the total left morphism to be the assumed projection.
            %p
              Next, by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of the top
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CellStructureOfKProjectiveSpace"}
            %p
