            %p
              Here the notation closely alludes to the construction inside the proof of Prop.
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CellStructureOfKProjectiveSpace"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1-r
              denotes a
              %em real
              number (regarded inside the complex numbers or quaternions under the chosen embedding above), using that there is always a homogeneous coordinate representative with the last entry of this form. With this understood, the maps are given by sending coordinate labels “to themselves”, and, if necessary, by including a last coordinate
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %mi r
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 - r = 0
            %p
